      <Docs>
        <summary>
          <para>When monitoring is enabled, the editor is requested to call <see cref="M:Android.Views.InputMethods.InputMethodManager.UpdateCursorAnchorInfo(Android.Views.View,Android.Views.InputMethods.CursorAnchorInfo)" /> with new character bounds from <see cref="M:Android.Views.InputMethods.CursorAnchorInfo.GetCharacterBounds(System.Int32)" /> whenever the cursor or anchor position changes. This filter selects the data to include. To disable monitoring, call <see cref="M:Android.Views.InputMethods.IInputConnection.RequestCursorUpdates(System.Int32)" /> without the <see cref="F:Android.Views.InputMethods.CursorUpdate.Monitor" /> bit.</para>
          <para>This flag can be combined with other <see cref="T:Android.Views.InputMethods.CursorUpdateFilter" /> values and the update flags <see cref="F:Android.Views.InputMethods.CursorUpdate.Immediate" /> and <see cref="F:Android.Views.InputMethods.CursorUpdate.Monitor" />.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/view/inputmethod/InputConnection#CURSOR_UPDATE_FILTER_CHARACTER_BOUNDS" title="Reference documentation">Android reference for <code>android.view.inputmethod.InputConnection.CURSOR_UPDATE_FILTER_CHARACTER_BOUNDS</code>.</a></format></para>
